 {
  "id": "2125468499887931526",
  "time": "Wed Nov 25 05:55:54 +0000 2026",
  "user": "TheMarketMemo",
  "name": "LEI",
  "text": "Every generation faces its share of crises: market crashes, wars, recessions, inflation, political upheaval, and endless negative news. Yet the stock market always trends upward over the long run.\n\nIf you are always waiting for the perfect moment to invest when there is world peace, economic prosperity, and absolute stability, you will either wait forever or end up buying right at the market peak. There are always crises, and there are always reasons to worry. \n\nMarket downturns are simply the entry ticket to long-term growth. If you want to succeed in the long run, you have to endure the journey. History shows that investors who keep putting money in while others are fearful consistently outperform those who wait on the sidelines and never pull the trigger. \n\nSuccessful investors reap rewards not by timing the market perfectly, but through patience and discipline.\n\n- LEI",
  "reply": 5,
  "like": 66,
  "rt": 3,
  "view": 4471,
  "lang": "en",
  "media": [],
  "url": "https://x.com/TheMarketMemo/status/2125468499887931526",
  "src": "fxtwitter-v2"
 },
